WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.970
If you want to hear about a kids movie clown
that scarred an entire generation, stick around

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:11.150
to the end of this video.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.090
So we've talked about horror movie clowns,
I've written you a creepy clown story and

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:20.340
short film, and it kind of begs the question,
are there ever any actual funny clowns who

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.300
aren't just horrifying?

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.539
I can only think of one really.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:27.360
But why ARE so many people afraid of clowns?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.560
Maybe they're just naturally scary, because
the makeup of a clown often contrasts and

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.950
hides their true facial expressions, tapping
into the fear of the unknown, kind of similar

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:37.530
to the fear of the dark.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:42.090
But maybe it's a deep seeded fear planted
from the point of childhood, because if you

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:48.130
look at some of the many clowns seen in kids
movies, there are some really disturbing ones.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:52.590
And most of them come from old Disney movies,
like Dumbo from 1941.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:56.559
This movie is about a circus elephant, so
you can bet there are a lot of clowns, but

00:00:56.559 --> 00:00:59.350
there's one scene in particular that stands
out.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.600
Dumbo has a dream about this parade of pink
elephants, which are already kind of creepy

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.430
with their empty eye sockets and Fauvism inspired
art style...

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:28.770
so when they start to appear as clowns, things
quickly break down into an acid trip nightmare.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.159
And as kind of a side note, I always think
the title at the end of the movie is also

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:33.159
pretty messed up.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.180
I mean look at that guy.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.520
It looks like he's crawling out from behind
that gong to feast on you.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.540
Of course, this is kind of an older movie
so I think that adds to the creep factor a

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.540
little bit.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:47.729
Another circus clown appearance can be seen
in Red's Dream, a PIXAR short from 1987.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:51.990
This was one of the earliest CG animated films
about a unicycle who dreams of being in the

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.630
circus, and what makes this so disturbing
is the level of detail and quality of animation

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.979
isn't quite what we're used to today.

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:03.579
It's just off-putting seeing this clown's
deformed face, and the way those balls float

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:05.680
in the air is unnatural.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.250
There's something off about the music, that
is, before the music just stops and he looks

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.739
directly into the camera.

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:23.169
That's just so creepy!

00:02:23.169 --> 00:02:27.870
The ending of this is really depressing for
a PIXAR film too, the dream ends and the unicycle

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.870
just cries in the corner for almost 30 seconds.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.829
Then it just ends.

00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:35.879
This clown also makes a little cameo in Toy
Story 2.

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:40.750
Another PIXAR clown appeared more recently
in 2015 with Inside Out when two of Riley's

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.129
emotions, Joy and Sadness try to sneak in
the part of her brain that contains her biggest

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:46.950
fears.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.769
*snoring*

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:52.670
The only thing scarier than a creepy clown,
is a giant creepy clown.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:57.159
Jangles seems to have been a birthday party
clown that psychologically scorned Riley.

00:02:57.159 --> 00:03:01.510
What makes him terrifying is similar to what
makes Pennywise so unnerving, which is the

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.629
fact that he's crazy and unpredictable.

00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:05.980
And did I mention giant?

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.230
This movie is more recent, so I wasn't a kid
when it came out, but if I had been, I'm sure

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.799
my nightmares would be filled with that laugh.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:13.799
"Birthday?!"

00:03:13.799 --> 00:03:14.799
"Oh man.

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:15.799
Follow us!"

00:03:15.799 --> 00:03:20.150
"Nothing like a good scare to wake you up,
right?"

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.279
Speaking of nightmare clowns, how did this
make it into a kids movie?

00:03:24.279 --> 00:03:28.379
A lot of kids are already afraid of going
to the doctor, so the fact that Pee Wee's

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:32.680
Big Adventure then takes that fear and throws
clowns into the mix is just not going to go

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.549
over well for them.

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:38.829
Not to mention that they seem to be using
torture devices to fix this bike and the whole

00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:47.239
dream devolves into some kind of nightmarish
hellscape.

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:59.019
"Ha, hahaha!"

00:03:59.019 --> 00:04:02.809
And moving right along from one nightmare
would to another, who could forget the Clown

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.790
with the Tear Away Face from Nightmare Before
Christmas?

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.510
"I am the clown with the tear-away face!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:12.010
Here in a flash and gone without a trace!"

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.729
The fact that the clown's true face is just
a black void is so disturbing compared to

00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:21.519
the other characters who simply have a spooky
form, like a skeleton, or a Boogeyman.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:26.069
It's not a scary movie despite being about
Halloween, but a clown with a black void under

00:04:26.069 --> 00:04:29.800
his face has become known the scariest part
of the movie for a lot of people who watched

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.220
this as kids.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.770
But the 90s clown horror does not end there.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.930
Air Bud of things, has a crazy clown in it.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:42.690
Like Jangles, it's the psychopathic tendencies
from a birthday clown that get you here.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:46.460
As soon as you see this rusty clown truck
come barreling over the hill to start the

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:49.020
movie, you know it means trouble...

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.740
Outside of the crudely applied makeup, one
thing that puts you on edge about this guy

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.310
is the evidence of anger issues.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.960
He is a bit less scary then some of the others
I've mentioned because of his clumsiness,

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.500
but there's still something off-putting about
a birthday clown who hates kids.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.500
"I HATE BIRTHDAY PARTIES!

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.979
I HATE KIDS!

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:11.110
I HATE BEING A CLOWN!"

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.389
There are also hints of alcoholism, which
can turn anyone into a monster, and the fact

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:19.189
that it's happening to a clown makes it that
much worse.

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:23.410
The next one is from a TV show, not a film,
but since Are You Afraid of the Dark is an

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:27.969
anthology series, it could really be considered
more of a collection of short films so I'm

00:05:27.969 --> 00:05:28.969
gonna count it.

00:05:28.969 --> 00:05:29.969
"Yeah!

00:05:29.969 --> 00:05:32.069
What kind of strange stuff happens on the
ride?"

00:05:32.069 --> 00:05:34.500
"Well that's what the kids wanted to know.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.280
Especially Wee-Gee!"

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.310
And also, it is intended to be scary for kids...

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.310
But you know what?

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.990
It's my channel, I can do what I want and
I'm talking about it!

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.669
Zeebo the Clown is from an episode called
"The Tale of Laughing in the Dark".

00:05:47.669 --> 00:05:52.770
Zeebo is actually the ghost of a runaway circus
clown who's cigarette butt started the fire

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:56.800
that ended his life while hiding out in an
amusement park spookhouse.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:59.669
This one definitely has the coolest backstory.

00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:03.479
And I always love some good creepy clown music.

00:06:03.479 --> 00:06:11.129
"It's the most fun in the park!

00:06:11.129 --> 00:06:12.330
When you're laughing..."

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:15.539
Zeebo plays more on suspense than it does
shock value.

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:19.509
We don't actually see the real ghost of Zeebo,
only this disturbing prop.

00:06:19.509 --> 00:06:24.500
But when Josh steals the clown's nose to prove
his bravery, Zeebo definitely begins to haunt

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.820
him at home.

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:30.520
It's never fully revealed if Zeebo's ghost
can be seen, or if this creepy carny who can

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:35.060
be seen smoking at the end is actually the
ghost of Zeebo out of makeup.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.689
One thing's for sure, I wouldn't want to be
the one to hear this clown's laughter in the

00:06:38.689 --> 00:06:39.689
dark.

00:06:39.689 --> 00:06:44.580
And finally, we have the creepiest clown to
have graced the screen of a kids movie.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:48.980
Have you noticed that 4/7 clowns so far have
appeared in nightmares?

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.020
That's probably not a coincidence.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.229
This last one is no exception.

00:06:53.229 --> 00:06:56.379
It comes from the 1987 Disney movie, The Brave
Little Toaster.

00:06:56.379 --> 00:07:00.300
A movie about five household appliances looking
for their old master.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.889
A movie that has no business being this creepy.

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:14.650
Just roll it.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:25.070
"Run."

00:07:25.070 --> 00:08:00.570
If they were trying to ruin every kid's childhood,
they got the design of this guy right, he

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:01.960
just looks sinister.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:06.150
You may have seen YouTuber Colossal is Crazy
repurpose this image to be his logo.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:11.060
The clown himself may actually be a reference
to the firefighter clowns from Dumbo, although

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.940
this is much scarier.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:17.680
Every thing from the lighting to the voice
to the towering perspective makes this clown

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:23.330
the stuff of every kid's nightmare, and to
top it all off, Disney always has to have

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:29.139
a dark side, and the suicide references suggested
by imagery of a fork in the toaster or a toaster

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:34.399
in the bathtub make this scene absolutely
chilling... and that's before you even get

00:08:34.399 --> 00:08:43.070
to the sound of the clown's creepy sadistic
laugh.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:52.600
If any of these clowns left a mark on your
childhood, be sure to give this video a like,

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.399
and go down to the comments to let me know
about any other creepy things you've seen

00:08:55.399 --> 00:08:56.790
in kids movies.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.750
If you're interested in topics like this,
check out some of my other Creepy Things videos

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:06.510
and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, ring that deathbell

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:09.880
for notifications and I'll see you in the
next one.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.750
Assuming we both survive.

